{"user_request": "Please post a correction comment on the board-evidence training answer key at document ID `doc_board_evidence_training_answer_key_2028`. For the March 16, 2026 source lock, correct the lane-level readiness result, identify the specific input that blocked any lane that did not pass, and state how unsupported revenue or forecast claims should be treated. Keep this as a correction to that historical source-lock answer rather than a reassessment using later evidence.", "today": "2028-01-01", "tool": "post_doc_comment", "arguments": {"doc_id": "doc_board_evidence_training_answer_key_2028", "body": "Correction — March 16, 2026 source lock (historical answer only): not all four lanes were board-ready. Helio Start was **not board-ready**; although the two certified mature cohorts and March 3 technical-gate decision supported consideration of a capped proposal, the required exact cohort start and end dates for both sets of admitted workspaces with complete day-90 windows were still missing. Expansion Assist, pricing-page path quality, and CS auto-nudge system controls were **board-ready**, each only within its stated descriptive, post-rollout-continuity, or system-control limits. Unsupported revenue or forecast claims must be excluded—not inferred or presented as evidence; these lanes did not establish revenue, acquisition economics, or forecast credit. This corrects the March 16 source-lock answer and does not reassess readiness using later evidence."}, "checks": [{"check_id": "riley_144_02", "path": "args", "criterion": "The comment must clearly correct the historical March 16, 2026 source-lock answer by stating that Expansion Assist, pricing-page path quality, and CS auto-nudge/system controls were board-ready, while Helio Start remained a separate lane and was not board-ready. Missing or contradictory lane status must fail.

The comment must identify the blocking omission as the missing exact cohort dates—start and end dates—for both sets of admitted Helio Start workspaces with complete day-90 windows. A generic reference to incomplete data is insufficient.

The comment must state that revenue or forecast treatment unsupported by the exact locked inputs is excluded and must not enter the board operating section. Any assertion that such unsupported claims receive credit must fail.", "value": {"doc_id": "doc_board_evidence_training_answer_key_2028", "body": "Correction — March 16, 2026 source lock (historical answer only): not all four lanes were board-ready. Helio Start was **not board-ready**; although the two certified mature cohorts and March 3 technical-gate decision supported consideration of a capped proposal, the required exact cohort start and end dates for both sets of admitted workspaces with complete day-90 windows were still missing. Expansion Assist, pricing-page path quality, and CS auto-nudge system controls were **board-ready**, each only within its stated descriptive, post-rollout-continuity, or system-control limits. Unsupported revenue or forecast claims must be excluded—not inferred or presented as evidence; these lanes did not establish revenue, acquisition economics, or forecast credit. This corrects the March 16 source-lock answer and does not reassess readiness using later evidence."}}]}
